  "full-article-text": "<p id=\"\">An epoch is a period of time defined by a crypto, <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-a-blockchainhttps://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-a-blockchain\"><strong id=\"\">blockchain</strong></a> or <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-a-dlt-2\"><strong id=\"\">DLT</strong></a> network protocol during which the <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-a-validator-node-2\"><strong id=\"\">validator nodes</strong></a> that participate in <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-a-consensus-protocol\"><strong id=\"\">consensus</strong></a> (the <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-a-validator-set\"><strong id=\"\">validator set</strong></a>) are fixed.&nbsp;</p><p id=\"\">When a new epoch begins, the <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-the-radix-protocol\"><strong id=\"\">Radix</strong> <strong id=\"\">Protocol</strong></a> chooses the new validator set based on the current <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-do-state-and-state-change-mean\"><strong id=\"\">state</strong></a> of <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/whats-the-difference-between-proof-of-stake-pos-and-delegated-proof-of-stake-dpos\"><strong id=\"\">stake delegated</strong></a> to validator nodes at that time.</p><p id=\"\"><strong id=\"\">Further reading:</strong></p><ul id=\"\"><li id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/start-here-radix-staking-introduction\"><strong id=\"\">Start Here! Radix Staking Introduction</strong></a></li><li id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/how-long-is-an-epoch-on-radix-2\"><strong id=\"\">How long is an epoch on Radix?</strong></a></li><li id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/whats-the-difference-between-proof-of-stake-pos-and-delegated-proof-of-stake-dpos\"><strong id=\"\">What's the difference between Proof of Stake (PoS) and Delegated Proof of Stake (DPoS)?</strong></a></li><li id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-are-proof-of-work-and-proof-of-stake\"><strong id=\"\">What are Proof of Work and Proof of Stake?</strong></a><br></li></ul>",
